      "message": "Overall, this looks good. Definitely like the structure of the new plumbed options. Just a couple nits on the review.\n\nAlso: Having `skslc` and `minify` built for the target platform is a mixed bag, in my opinion. Realistically, I don\u0027t think it will cause any problems - anyone building/running those tools is doing so on a build for their own local machine (or similarly, it\u0027s part of a host \u003d\u003d target build on the check-generated-files jobs). In the wacky world of bazel future, it also means that skslc can function even more like a test-binary (so you could run and debug skslc to test codegen independent of everything else, on whatever target platform you\u0027re interested in). Overall, I think it\u0027s okay, but thanks for adding the comments to the bzl files.",
